window.NEWS_DATA.en = {"three":[{"t":"U.S. stocks fall sharply, and the Nasdaq drops almost 3%","x":"In New York on the 30th, the Dow fell 572 dollars, and the Nasdaq, which has many tech stocks, fell almost 3%. Shares of the chip maker Intel fell about 30% after its earnings report, and people were also disappointed by Amazon's earnings. People worry that big spending on AI will take longer to make money (Nikkei, Kyodo, Jiji, TheStreet). This may also affect Tokyo stocks next week (Nov. 2), especially chip and AI companies."},{"t":"Very strong Typhoon No. 31 moves near the Ogasawara Islands and may stay for days","x":"Typhoon No. 31 is \"very strong,\" with a central pressure of 940 hPa. It will move near the Ogasawara Islands on the 31st and slow down. The Japan Meteorological Agency says the Ogasawara Islands may be in the storm area around Nov. 1 to 4 (JMA on the 30th at 18:45, tenki.jp, Weathernews). Even if it does not come near Honshu, waves may be high on the Pacific side. In Kanto, be careful of sudden rain and strong gusts until late morning on the 31st."},{"t":"Four big banks will lower fixed home loan rates in November","x":"Four big banks will lower their fixed interest rates for home loans in November, because long-term interest rates have stopped rising so fast (NHK, Kyodo, Jiji). On the 30th, the Bank of Japan kept its rate at 1.25%, and Governor Ueda said it will decide on a rate rise \"including at the next meeting (December)\" (NHK, Kyodo). This matters to people who plan to buy a home or change their loan."}],"top10":[{"t":"U.S. stocks fall sharply as worries about AI spending grow","x":"In New York on the 30th, the Dow fell 572 dollars, and the Nasdaq fell almost 3%, at one point more than 1,000 points (Nikkei, Kyodo, Jiji, TheStreet). Intel fell about 30% after its earnings, and Amazon also fell (Nikkei, Quartz, Yahoo Finance). People worry that big spending on AI will take longer to make money. On the 29th, Alphabet had also fallen about 12%.","w":[["sharply","大きく"],["earnings","決算"]]},{"t":"Up to 27.26 million records at Muji, and travel bookings at JAL and ANA: data leaks continue","x":"On the evening of the 30th, Muji (Ryohin Keikaku) said up to about 27.26 million records, such as email addresses and birthdays, may have leaked from its official app (NHK, Nikkei, Kyodo, Jiji, ITmedia). About 2.38 million records leaked from the Matsuya Foods app. JAL and ANA also said booking information was accessed through an overseas contractor. On the night of the 30th, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs said about 3,600 records, such as email addresses and names, may have leaked (Jiji, Kyodo, TBS, Yomiuri).","w":[["leak","漏れる"],["contractor","委託先"]]},{"t":"Very strong Typhoon No. 31 moves near Ogasawara, with storms possible Nov. 1-4","x":"At 3 p.m. on the 30th, Typhoon No. 31 had a central pressure of 940 hPa and gusts of 65 meters per second. It will move near the Ogasawara Islands on the 31st and slow down (tenki.jp, Weathernews). The Japan Meteorological Agency said the islands may be in the storm area around Nov. 1 to 4 (RKK). Its path after the 5th is still uncertain.","w":[["typhoon","台風"],["gust","突風・瞬間風速"]]},{"t":"Four big banks will lower fixed home loan rates in November","x":"Four big banks will lower their fixed rates for home loans in November, because long-term interest rates have stopped rising so fast (NHK, Kyodo, Jiji).","w":[["home loan","住宅ローン"],["fixed rate","固定金利"]]},{"t":"About 6.3 billion dollars stolen from the big crypto exchange Binance, the largest ever","x":"About 6.3 billion dollars (about 980 billion yen) was stolen from Binance, a big exchange for crypto assets. It is the largest ever. North Korean hackers are suspected (TechCrunch, CNN, CBS, Al Jazeera, CNBC).","w":[["steal","盗む"],["exchange","取引所"]]},{"t":"New York oil ends at over 104 dollars, the highest in a month and a half","x":"On the 30th, New York oil ended at over 104 dollars, the highest in a month and a half. Worries about the Middle East continue (Kyodo, Nikkei, Minkabu).","w":[["oil","原油"],["highest","いちばん高い"]]},{"t":"In the last days before the U.S. midterm elections (Nov. 3), President Trump stops in-person rallies","x":"In the last days before the U.S. midterm elections on Nov. 3, President Trump stopped holding rallies in person and switched to calling people by phone. Some think the Republican Party is having a hard time (Kyodo, The Washington Post).","w":[["election","選挙"],["rally","集会"]]},{"t":"In Israel's election, the prime minister's party says \"the election was stolen\"","x":"In Israel's general election, Prime Minister Netanyahu's party says \"the election was stolen.\" It was reported that the police have not found evidence of cheating (this is the prime minister's side's claim; Anadolu, JTA, Axios).","w":[["claim","主張する"],["evidence","証拠"]]},{"t":"Today is Halloween; in Shibuya, the Hachiko statue is fenced off and traffic is limited","x":"Today is Halloween, and it falls on a Saturday for the first time in 6 years. In Shibuya, the Hachiko statue is fenced off, and there are traffic limits on the 30th and 31st. The police are on high alert (NTV, ANN, FNN).","w":[["statue","像"],["traffic","交通"]]},{"t":"Flu patients rise a little again across Japan, to 9.49 per medical facility","x":"The number of flu patients rose a little again across Japan. In the week of Oct. 19-25, there were 9.49 patients per medical facility. Ehime Prefecture had the most (NHK, ReseMom).","w":[["flu","インフルエンザ"],["patient","患者"]]}],"ex":{"saudi":"In the Middle East, an armed group and Saudi Arabia keep fighting, and oil prices are rising. This connects to gas prices in Japan.","tax":"A plan to lower the tax on food you buy at the supermarket from 8% to 1%. It has not been decided yet.","cyber":"Bad actors keep breaking into the computers of companies and government offices and stealing information such as names and addresses.","mmx":"A Japanese probe has left for Mars. The plan is to bring back sand from a small moon near Mars.","sato":"The Hanshin Tigers agreed to let Sato, this year's \"Triple Crown\" hitter, try to play in Major League Baseball in America.","series":"SoftBank beat DeNA 4 games in a row and became Japan's champion for the second year in a row (10/28).","yokohama":"There was an election to choose the leader (mayor) of Yokohama, and a new person was chosen.","past":"Three weeks of worries about a big typhoon and a volcano, a new governor of Okinawa and new ministers, and higher interest rates in America.","ukr":"Talks to end the war between Russia and Ukraine may be held in Abu Dhabi on November 6-10. A small ceasefire has also started in one town.","typhoon":"Typhoon No. 30 changed into an extratropical low on the night of the 25th. On the 26th, heavy rain is possible from Kyushu to Kanto.","shogi":"Shogi player Tomoka Nishiyama decided to become a \"kishi,\" the professional player status open to both men and women. In April next year she will be the first woman kishi in shogi history.","reporter":"A Japanese newspaper reporter was arrested in Russia as a \"spy.\" The Japanese government says he is not a spy and asks Russia to send him home soon.","hamaoka":"Local residents went to court asking to stop the Hamaoka nuclear plant in Shizuoka, but the court dismissed the case.","israel":"There was a parliament election in Israel, and the prime minister's side may not win more than half of the seats.","teisu":"Political parties are talking about whether to reduce the number of members of the House of Representatives.","fed":"America's central bank (the Fed) decided not to change its main interest rate, and the Bank of Japan also kept its rate the same.","cold":"Cold air like in winter came, it snowed in the north, and the morning of the 29th was the coldest of this fall.","typhoon31":"A very strong typhoon may stay for many days near the Ogasawara Islands, south of Tokyo, while moving slowly."}};
